      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T08:50:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if the already-shared pages are passed again e.g.\n```\nlet mut total \u003d 0;\nwhile (total \u003c n_granules) {\n    total +\u003d mmio_guard_map(base, n_granules)?;\n}\n```\ninstead of\n```\nwhile (n_granules \u003e 0) {\n    let n \u003d mmio_guard_map(base, n_granules)?;\n    n_granules -\u003d n;\n    base +\u003d n * granule_size;\n}\n```\n?\n\nCould you specify in the docs that the `n` pages that the HVC returns having shared can only be the \"first\" ones (in IPA order) of the range?\n\nAlso, there must be a guarantee that `n` is never 0 i.e. that the first page is always shared, for compatibility with guests that don\u0027t support `KVM_FUNC_HAS_RANGE` (which would see that R0 is `RET_SUCCESS`, ignoring R1). As a result, this also gives a guarantee to guests that do support it that the loops above always terminate. If I\u0027m not wrong, could this also be mentioned?\n\nIMO, it would be worth discussing this details once in a paragraph/section then point to it from the 4 individual ranged HVC docs.",
